## Comparative results and public preservation

The fourth Metrics wrapper campaign has147 timing and147 isolated-memory children; its root audit independently authenticates882 raw logs,1,835 numeric PID samples and recomputes441 statistics without new measurements. All-percentile paired median timing is−11.066% but three of seven pairs are slower and timing ranges overlap. Single-p95 lifetime RSS rises from79.395MiB to82.484MiB. Signed negative controls,686 unavailable zero-control percentages and prior regressions remain. Baseline reducer is unchanged and the candidate is unaccepted. [Wrapper observations](results/metrics-wrapper-observations-20261012/README.md) and its prospective diagnostic plan do not imply uniform improvement or another executed experiment.

Notes maps935 source/self-carrier records to920 public inert snapshots and15 copies of one local synthetic TAR/JEX carrier. Vault maps858 records to857 public aliases/471 unique objects (444 new,27 exact reuse) and one local synthetic KDBX carrier. Editor Save maps516 records to174 public source objects (101new,73 reuse). Four Vault screenshots retain original.png aliases despite JPEG headers; exact image bytes are preserved. Local Windows path/username metadata and original source attribution remain explicit. Native vendor executables/full archives/private caches remain local. Root installation collector failures and proposed-source adapter differences are retained; finite scans are not proof of absence of every secret, personal datum or supply-chain risk.

The next phase continues implementing the missing contracts, beginning with an accessible in-page Notes confirmation and broader release-bound editor compatibility. No completion notification is warranted.

Publication validation found the installed Notes README pointed to a notice absent from the original stage epoch. A [separately recorded exact documentation alias](results/notebook-trash-notice-link-repair-20261013/repair.json) now exposes the authentic publication-correction notice at that link. The original 935 source records and 920 mapped snapshots stay unchanged; this one added alias is excluded from their historical counts. All 709 test-source identities remain exact.
